 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "But I am our Lord, alone,\nThe marvellous heart of only.\nI have love in me, knoweth never,\nYea, the soul that had breath to feel however,\nAnd yet hath love for myself.\nLove is within us everywhere,\nA spirit passing into being there;\nYet my love's still not ours anywhere.\nMy love, too, in nature remains,\nFinds no flower or leaf again,\nNor on his surface's lustre resides,\nOr one a-dreaming of himself decides.",
